---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
const toc = [
  ['summary', 'The short version'],
  ['hosting', 'Hosting'],
  ['analytics', 'Page views and actions (PostHog)'],
  ['price-check', 'The price check'],
  ['email-forms', 'Email forms'],
  ['emails', 'Emails we send'],
  ['payments', 'Payments'],
  ['email-us', 'When you email us'],
  ['sharing', 'Selling and sharing'],
  ['retention', 'How long we keep it'],
  ['choices', 'Leaving the list and deletion'],
  ['sponsored', 'Sponsored placements'],
  ['children', 'Children'],
  ['changes', 'Changes to this policy'],
  ['contact', 'Contact'],
];
---
<Base title="Privacy policy" description="What aiphonecompare collects and why: anonymous PostHog page views with no tracking cookie, optional email forms stored in Supabase, emails sent with Resend, and payments through Stripe.">
  <article class="wrap prose page-intro legal">
    <h1>Privacy policy</h1>
    <p class="note">Last updated: November 13, 2026</p>
    <nav class="legal-toc" aria-label="On this page">
      <h2 id="toc-heading">On this page</h2>
      <ol>
        {toc.map(([id, label]) => <li><a href={`#${id}`}>{label}</a></li>)}
      </ol>
    </nav>

    <h2 id="summary">The short version</h2>
    <p>You can use aiphonecompare without an account. We count anonymous page views and a few actions (pay-button clicks, contact and vendor-link clicks, tool use, and form sends), never with your email or name. If you choose to give us your email address, we use it to send what you asked for and the list you joined. If you buy a spotlight, Stripe handles the card. We do not sell personal information, and we do not use it for advertising.</p>

    <h2 id="hosting">Hosting</h2>
    <p>The site is a set of static pages hosted on GitHub Pages. To serve a page, GitHub receives standard request data, such as your IP address and browser details. GitHub handles that data under <a href="https://docs.github.com/en/site-policy/privacy-policies/github-general-privacy-statement">its own privacy statement</a>.</p>

    <h2 id="analytics">Page views and actions (PostHog)</h2>
    <p>We use <a href="https://posthog.com/">PostHog</a> (its US cloud, us.i.posthog.com) to count anonymous page views and a few actions: clicks on pay buttons, contact links, and vendor or referral links, and when someone uses a comparison tool or sends a form. A page view includes the page address and the basic technical details PostHog sends with that request. An action may also include the offer or tool name, a price tier, a vendor slug, or the form's source and industry. We do not ask you to sign in, and we do not attach these counts to your name. Your email and name are never sent to PostHog.</p>
    <p>The counter keeps its id in memory for the page session. It does not set a tracking cookie.</p>
    <p>If your browser sends Do Not Track, we do not start PostHog.</p>
    <p>Autocapture (recording every click) and session recording are turned off. We only record the actions named above, not every click on the page.</p>

    <h2 id="price-check">The price check</h2>
    <p>The <a href="/overpaying/">price check</a> runs in your browser. It counts that a check was run, with the industry, a rough cost band, and how many plans came in lower. A shared result link keeps the industry and numbers in the page address, and the page address is part of a page view. Your email and name are never sent to PostHog.</p>

    <h2 id="email-forms">Email forms</h2>
    <p>These forms on the site ask for an email address. Each one is optional.</p>
    <ul>
      <li><strong>"Email me the results" on the price check.</strong> We store your email, the optional first name and business name, the numbers from that check, and the top matches shown to you.</li>
      <li><strong>The stories list on the <a href="/stories/">stories page</a>.</strong> We store your email and the industry you pick.</li>
      <li><strong>The free missed-call audit form.</strong> We store your name, business name, business website, business phone number, industry and email. We use them to place one short test call to that number and to email you the report, and we keep a one-way hash of the phone number for up to 2 days to limit repeat requests.</li>
    </ul>
    <p>All of these forms send to the same place: a <a href="https://supabase.com/">Supabase</a> Edge Function that saves the signup in a Supabase database table in a US region. The public can't read that table. Your email stays in that table. PostHog is only told that a form was sent, with the form's source and industry, never the email or phone number.</p>
    <p>We also store your browser's user-agent (the short text that names your browser and system) with the signup. To limit abuse, we make a one-way hash of your IP address. That hash is used only to rate-limit repeated sign-ups and is kept for up to 2 days. We do not store the IP address itself.</p>

    <h2 id="emails">Emails we send</h2>
    <p>We send email with <a href="https://resend.com/">Resend</a>, from timothy@aiphonecompare.com.</p>
    <ul>
      <li>After you sign up, a welcome email: your price check results, or a note confirming the stories list you joined, or a confirmation of your missed-call audit followed by its report.</li>
      <li>For the stories list, new stories and logged price changes for the industry you picked.</li>
      <li>For the price check list, occasional price updates.</li>
    </ul>
    <p>Our own inbox gets a short notice of each new signup.</p>

    <h2 id="payments">Payments</h2>
    <p>The $49 Industry spotlight on the <a href="/get-featured/">get featured page</a> is paid through Stripe Payment Links. <a href="https://stripe.com/">Stripe</a> collects your card and billing details. We never see full card numbers.</p>
    <p>From Stripe we receive the buyer's email, name, the amount paid, and Stripe's payment IDs. We store them with the order record in the same Supabase table, and we send a thank-you email. Refunds are covered by the <a href="/refunds/">refund policy</a>.</p>

    <h2 id="email-us">When you email us</h2>
    <p>If you email or reply to timothy@aiphonecompare.com, your message is kept in that mailbox.</p>

    <h2 id="sharing">Selling and sharing</h2>
    <p>We do not sell personal information. We do not use it for advertising. The services named on this page (GitHub, PostHog, Supabase, Resend, and Stripe) handle data only to do the jobs described here.</p>

    <h2 id="retention">How long we keep it</h2>
    <p>List subscribers are kept until they leave the list or ask us to delete their record. Payment records are kept as long as we need them for accounting.</p>

    <h2 id="choices">Leaving the list and deletion</h2>
    <p>To leave a list, reply to any email we send. To have your record deleted, email <a href="mailto:timothy@aiphonecompare.com">timothy@aiphonecompare.com</a> and we will delete it.</p>

    <h2 id="sponsored">Sponsored placements</h2>
    <p>Sponsored placements are labeled on the page. They are separate from these traffic counts. Payment does not change listed prices or the order of unsponsored listings.</p>

    <h2 id="children">Children</h2>
    <p>aiphonecompare is for businesses. It is not directed to children.</p>

    <h2 id="changes">Changes to this policy</h2>
    <p>If we change how the site handles data, we update this page and the date at the top.</p>

    <h2 id="contact">Contact</h2>
    <p>Questions about privacy: <a href="mailto:timothy@aiphonecompare.com">timothy@aiphonecompare.com</a>.</p>
  </article>
</Base>
